    "body": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/path/struct.Path.html#method.has_root\r\n\r\n```\r\nReturns true if the Path has a root.\r\n\r\n    On Unix, a path has a root if it begins with /.\r\n\r\n    On Windows, a path has a root if it:\r\n        has no prefix and begins with a separator, e.g., \\windows\r\n        has a prefix followed by a separator, e.g., c:\\windows but not c:windows\r\n        has any non-disk prefix, e.g., \\\\server\\share\r\n```\r\n\r\nThought that rather making an object that's just going to check the first character, I would just check the first character.\r\n\r\nI'll change it though.",
